{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain of the function  $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is given by the expression\n\n$$\nx\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x\\ne n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & \\ne n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80bcbfbbe20a307f9ec9360a16e76d17ba901b2790de6b2814cb839a53612d33"} {"question" "q-10404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{n\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{n\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ne \\frac{n\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+1?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+1,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{x}{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{3} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80bcbfbbe20a307f9ec9360a16e76d17ba901b2790de6b2814cb839a53612d33"} {"question" "q-10406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ne \\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi "] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{3\\pi }{2}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+4n\\pi "] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{8}+n\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-10406" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ne \\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-29352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)+2?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-29352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)+2,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-29352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80bcbfbbe20a307f9ec9360a16e76d17ba901b2790de6b2814cb839a53612d33"} {"question" "q-29352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-29352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-29352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80bcbfbbe20a307f9ec9360a16e76d17ba901b2790de6b2814cb839a53612d33"} {"question" "q-81542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi n"] ["math" "4\\pi n"] ["math" "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{n\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{n\\pi }{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi x}{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}+n \\\\ x & =1+2n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=1+2n,$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80bcbfbbe20a307f9ec9360a16e76d17ba901b2790de6b2814cb839a53612d33"} {"question" "q-81557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=1+2n"] ["math" "x=2+n"] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\pi +2n\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"} {"question" "q-81557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=1+2n"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963074/state.json" "file_sha256" "68a42522b7fed75352fed5477e59431703d597bb12595089d63724ac76b3e90f"}] "usage" {"q-29352" [] "q-10404" []} "basis" 753 "retractions" [[17592186129338 :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $f(x) = 2\\cot (3x)$? Assume that $n$ is an integer."